    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46573" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sum-mŏnĕo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subm-</span></b> ), ŭi,
		2, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to remind privily</i>, <i>give a
			hint</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">summonuit me Parmeno, quod, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 3, 5, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patres salutavit nominatim singulos, nullo
					summonente,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 53</span></i>
			.</div>
